# Automatic model-scoped T1 S3 handling (0.6)

Target for both the current installation and public project: the supported
MacBookPro14,3 driver performs its normal S3 work without an enable parameter,
one-cycle mode or repeat mode. System sleep policy decides whether suspend is
available. No new suspend, reboot or driver live reload is authorized here.

Based on preserved 0.5. Removed `s3_notify_once` and `s3_notify_repeat`; the
MacBookPro14,3 DMI quirk selects the existing ordered firmware path automatically.
Other models do not enter this S3 firmware path. The legacy probe/runtime SOCW
freeze guard remains separate and unchanged. The existing skip setting is not
an activation requirement for the new S3 path; it protects old call sites.

The same state machine serializes firmware notifications with Touch Bar I/O,
requires a real firmware return and completed cache refresh before the next
transaction, and reports terminal transaction errors. Those checks protect
driver consistency; they do not implement a user one-cycle/repeat policy.
Read-only diagnostics are `s3_status` (0 initial/ready, 1 active, 2 pending
refresh, 3 failed, 4 completed) and `s3_completed`. There is no reset/arming knob.

Actual-C tests cover five automatic cycles with no activation state, DMI scope,
firmware/USB failures, abort, missing interfaces and a threaded cache-commit race.
This is source verification, not hardware acceptance. Earlier five controlled
and two personal cycles belong to 0.5, not this revision.

Keep old tickets, signed 0.5, boot metadata and image for rollback. Do not use
old one-shot runners or legacy option-bearing entries with the new module.
Activation requires a planned normal reboot and updated system readiness/boot
configuration. No hardware PM test is included in preparing this candidate.
